      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The shift toward automation is not a neutral technological inevitability but a deliberate strategy driven by corporate greed and government deregulation designed to maximize profits at the expense of workers. While technology provides the tools, it is the political will of both parties to prioritize shareholder value over labor rights that has accelerated this transition so rapidly. Framing this as an unavoidable evolution ignores the fact that policy choices like tax incentives for automation and the erosion of union power have actively engineered this outcome.",
