    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>That's a pretty strong take. You're saying it's basically a political decision rather than something just happening because the tech exists. But wouldn't you say that even with different policies, the fundamental trajectory of technological advancement—the math and the engineering behind it—is still going to push us toward automation regardless? Like, once the efficiency makes sense, isn't it somewhat inevitable?",
